<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  macOS launchd agent: collect NZ term-deposit market rates once a day.

  Sibling of nz.pricing-intelligence.collect.plist (the home-loan schedule).
  Term deposits are a separate market, selected via the product flag below
  (term_deposit); this file's lock-file and summary-file paths are
  deliberately distinct from the home-loan schedule's, so an overlapping run
  of one product cannot make the workflow skip the other
  (EXIT_ALREADY_RUNNING) or overwrite its summary file.

  The lock-file argument below matches exactly what
  orchestration.default_lock_file_path() itself computes for the config
  flag's configs/base.yaml (unconfigured, so default) database path;
  explicit here rather than relying on that default so an interactive
  `pricing-intelligence run` with the product flag set to term_deposit
  against the same database always shares this same lock. If you configure
  a different pricing_intelligence.database_path, update this path to
  match.

  Install (in addition to the home-loan plist):
    cp deploy/scheduling/nz.pricing-intelligence.collect-term-deposit.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    # Edit the two REPLACE_ME paths below first.
    # launchd opens StandardOutPath/StandardErrorPath itself before it even
    # starts the program below, so on a fresh checkout (where this git-ignored
    # directory does not exist yet) load fails silently unless it exists first:
    mkdir -p /path/to/ai-bank-pricing-engine/data/processed/pricing_intelligence
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nz.pricing-intelligence.collect-term-deposit.plist

  Check / run now / remove:
    launchctl list | grep pricing-intelligence
    launchctl start nz.pricing-intelligence.collect-term-deposit
    launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/nz.pricing-intelligence.collect-term-deposit.plist

  Scheduled five minutes after the home-loan run (07:35 local) so the two
  schedules don't start at the exact same instant. They use independent
  lock files and could run concurrently regardless, but staggering keeps
  their logs easier to read.

  The config flag below (configs/base.yaml) is passed explicitly: without
  it, the workflow falls back to PricingIntelligenceConfig() defaults and
  silently ignores any pricing_intelligence block (selected banks,
  validation thresholds, collection delays, database path) configured
  there.

  Optional alert delivery: environment variables are scoped per plist, so
  the home-loan plist's EnvironmentVariables block does not extend to this
  agent; add the same block here too if you also want term-deposit rate
  moves pushed to Slack, Teams, Discord, and/or Telegram. (launchd does not
  inherit your shell's exported variables, so `export ...` before
  `launchctl load` has no effect on the child process; it must go in the
  plist itself.)

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PRICING_INTELLIGENCE_ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL</key>
        <string>https://hooks.slack.com/services/T000/B000/xxxx</string>
        <key>TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN</key>
        <string>123456:AAAA-your-bot-token</string>
        <key>TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID</key>
        <string>-1001234567890</string>
    </dict>

  Add it as a sibling of ProgramArguments below. Each is independent;
  configure any subset. These are secrets, so keep them out of the copy of
  this file under version control; only the installed copy in
  ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ should carry real values. Leave a variable unset
  (the default) for no delivery on that channel; nothing else about
  collection changes either way, and a broken channel never fails the run.
  End-to-end deadline (DATA-008): the run-timeout-seconds argument below
  (1800 s = 30 min) bounds this product's whole collection. The workflow
  runs the collection in a supervised worker process; past the deadline the
  supervisor terminates the worker and its Chromium processes (SIGTERM, then
  SIGKILL after a 10 s grace), writes a collection_timeout summary to the
  summary file, records a FAILED run when the database allows, releases the
  lock, and exits 1. The default worst case for five banks that never hang
  is about 21 minutes (docs/pricing_intelligence.md, "Collection deadline"),
  so 30 minutes targets genuine hangs only. ExitTimeOut gives that
  supervisor time to stop its worker if launchd itself stops the job.

  Repeated exit 3 (already running) is escalated per product: a warning at 2
  consecutive skips, one alert per configured channel at 3, and a recovery
  notice once the lock is acquired again. State lives beside the lock file
  (lock file name + ".skips.json").
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>nz.pricing-intelligence.collect-term-deposit</string>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>REPLACE_ME/ai-bank-pricing-engine</string>

    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>REPLACE_ME/ai-bank-pricing-engine/.venv/bin/python3</string>
        <string>scripts/collect_market_rates_workflow.py</string>
        <string>--config</string>
        <string>configs/base.yaml</string>
        <string>--product</string>
        <string>term_deposit</string>
        <string>--render-javascript</string>
        <string>--quiet</string>
        <string>--run-timeout-seconds</string>
        <string>1800</string>
        <string>--lock-file</string>
        <string>data/processed/pricing_intelligence/collection-term-deposit-observations.lock</string>
        <string>--summary-file</string>
        <string>data/processed/pricing_intelligence/last_run_term_deposit.json</string>
    </array>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key><integer>7</integer>
        <key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer>
    </dict>

    <!-- Seconds launchd waits after SIGTERM before SIGKILL when stopping this job:
         longer than the supervisor's 10 s grace for its worker. -->
    <key>ExitTimeOut</key>
    <integer>30</integer>

    <!-- Catch up if the machine was asleep at the scheduled time. -->
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <true/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>REPLACE_ME/ai-bank-pricing-engine/data/processed/pricing_intelligence/collect.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>REPLACE_ME/ai-bank-pricing-engine/data/processed/pricing_intelligence/collect.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
